{"name":"Humidor","hex":"#6d5843","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"humidor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A container designed to keep its contents at a constant humidity; especially such a box for storing cigars."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/humidor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Humidor","blocks":[{"text":"A humidor is a humidity-controlled box or room used primarily for storing cigars, cigarettes, cannabis, or pipe tobacco. Either too much or too little humidity can be harmful to tobacco products; a humidor's primary function is to maintain a steady, desirable moisture level inside; secondarily it protects its contents from physical damage and deterioration from sunlight. For private use, small wooden boxes holding a few dozen or fewer cigars are common, while cigar shops may have walk-in humidors. Many humidors use hygrometers to monitor their humidity levels. When used and maintained properly, humidors can keep cigars fresh and in perfect condition for decades."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Humidor_Vorbereitung.jpg/330px-Humidor_Vorbereitung.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humidor","wikidata":"Q921455"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Humidor_Vorbereitung.jpg/500px-Humidor_Vorbereitung.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Humidor_Vorbereitung.jpg/500px-Humidor_Vorbereitung.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Humidor with hygrometer and bowl of water during initial seasoning","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHumidor_Vorbereitung.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Humidor.jpg/500px-Humidor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten